## 3. Participants

### 3.1 Peppol Access Point (Corner 4)

Sends signed EN 16931 invoice data to Corner 5. Standard Peppol participant with no changes to existing infrastructure.

### 3.2 DTEP-F Corner 5 Middleware

The central component. Receives data from Corner 4, executes Layers 3–5, transmits DRR records to DRRDB and the analytical layer.

### 3.3 GNU Taler Exchange

Signing authority for Layer 4. Generates coin commitments for M0 and signs public DTEP JSON objects.

### 3.4 DRRDB

Digital Reporting Requirements Database. Layered storage built on the Taler auditor protocol.

- **Public level:** accessible for Central VIES queries without specific rights
- **Protected level:** accessible to the business entity via EUDI Wallet and to the tax authority on audit trigger

### 3.5 Tax Administration

Receives DRR data from the public level of DRRDB in real time. On combined fraud signal receives an Audit Request to the protected level.

### 3.6 Business Entity (buyer / seller)

Not an active participant in the protocol chain. Receives an optional Taler wallet interface for B2B payment bound to M0 — not as an obligation but as a service layer closing DRR obligation and payment in one action.

