## 6. Deployment Scenarios

DTEP-F supports graceful degradation under partial adoption. Each scenario is independently viable.

### Scenario 1 — Full chain

Peppol Access Point sends directly to DTEP-F Corner 5 Middleware. DRR records enter in real time. Taler Exchange is online. Analytical layer operates continuously.

### Scenario 2 — Batch mode

Corner 5 Middleware operates offline. DRR records accumulate locally and are transmitted to DRRDB in batches. Taler Exchange signing executes on reconnection. Cryptographic integrity is maintained throughout the offline period.

### Scenario 3 — Legacy Peppol input adapter

Existing Peppol Access Point without changes. DTEP-F adapter receives standard AS4 stream and normalises it before Layer 3. Upgrades automatically on direct Corner 5 implementation.

### Scenario 4 — Analytical layer only

Existing DRR data from a legacy system imported as DTEP-F public objects. Analytical layer activates immediately. Full chain enabled incrementally.

In all scenarios, DRR records are cryptographically signed and immutable once generated. No retroactive data migration is required when new participants are added.

