## 7. Privacy and Data Protection

Subject identifiers are processed exclusively in Layer 3 through DD-18 scrubbing. In the public level of DRRDB and the analytical layer, subject identifiers are absent — not pseudonymised, but structurally excluded.

The key privacy property of the temporal ontology: time nodes in M1 are not personal data under any GDPR definition. The adjacency matrix T × T contains no subject information regardless of the number of taxpayers in the system.

The full encrypted JSON artifact contains original identifiers in scrubbed form — accessible only to the tax authority on audit trigger via EUDI Wallet with appropriate rights.

Legal bases: Article 6(1)(c) GDPR — compliance with legal obligation (ViDA DRR); Article 6(1)(e) GDPR — public interest task. No special category data is processed in the public layer.

See [docs/gdpr-analysis.md](../docs/gdpr-analysis.md) for full analysis.

