## 8. Security Considerations

**Unforgeability:** DRR records are signed by Taler Exchange. A valid record cannot be produced without Exchange participation.

**Unlinkability:** M0 coin commitment ensures that an observer cannot link two DRRDB records to the same invoice without access to Taler Exchange — even with knowledge of the invoice identifier.

**Replay prevention:** Each DRR record carries a unique UUID and timestamp. DRRDB validates against duplication index on receipt.

**Carousel fraud detection:** τ(H) acyclicity verification is deterministic — a cycle in the temporal hypergraph is a physically impossible event under normal commerce, not a probabilistic anomaly.

**Offline integrity:** Batch mode maintains cryptographic integrity throughout. Signing deferred to reconnection does not affect record validity.

See [docs/threat-model.md](../docs/threat-model.md) for full threat model.

